# Target: Cloudflare Workers + D1 + R2 + Workflows + Clerk + Meta Model API.
# Migration/configuration wiring is not implemented yet.
# This file intentionally does not prescribe environment variable names until
# the consuming code and compatible SDK configuration are established.
#
# Public configuration: Clerk publishable key and approved application origin.
# Server secrets: Clerk backend key, optional webhook signing secret, and
# Meta Model API credential. Never expose these through VITE_ variables.
#
# Exact variable names (values stay in ignored local files, never in Git):
#   .env.local  -> VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   (pk_test_... / pk_live_...)
#   .dev.vars   -> CLERK_SECRET_KEY             (sk_test_... / sk_live_...)
#   .dev.vars   -> CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET (whsec_..., when webhooks land)
#   .dev.vars   -> META_API_KEY
# Production: set the three server secrets as Worker secrets with the
# Cloudflare cf CLI or dashboard. Do not put them in wrangler.jsonc or GitHub.
#
# Proposed Worker bindings (not environment-variable connection strings):
# DB              -> Cloudflare D1
# TAILOR_MEDIA    -> private Cloudflare R2 bucket
# TAILOR_WORKFLOW -> Cloudflare Workflow
#
# Configure local/deployed bindings through the Cloudflare cf CLI setup once
# implemented. Do not paste legacy Supabase or PostgreSQL migration credentials
# here. Keep all actual credentials in ignored local files or managed secrets.
